 INFRASTRUCTURE_BLOCKED, real gate result obtained

Re-ran the bounded-reinduction A/B (conductor + orphan-cleanup timer stopped
for the duration) after the prior four launches produced zero valid cells.
All 4 cells completed on the first attempt, all valid, real nonzero LLM
responses throughout. Lever fires as designed on both games
(renewed_stall_reinduction: 2 each) but reached_any_level stayed false on
both arms of both games -- a clean negative, not an infra non-result.
CARNOT_ARC_BOUNDED_REINDUCTION stays default OFF; n=2 games too thin to
flip a default even on a clean result.

Second correlational instance this session linking conductor-concurrent
operation to reaper crash frequency (explicitly correlational, no causal
mechanism identified). Appended to REQ-ARC-WMTE-6247 and known-issues.md
without overwriting the prior INFRASTRUCTURE_BLOCKED record.

Also fixed a real bug found during commit review: the script never set
CARNOT_ARC_E3_DIR, so it wrote induced engines straight into the shared
results/arc_e3/{ka59,re86} store, clobbering the conductor's own
accumulated state (caught only because the conductor happened to be
stopped). Reverted those two files via git checkout and isolated the
script to a private scratch dir for future runs.

